  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to the electrochemical series</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>/</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>93</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Rb</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>/</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Rb</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>98</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>/</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Na</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>71</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Li</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>/</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Li</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>Among the given alkali metals, sodium metal is the weakest reducing agent as its standard reduction potential is least&nbsp;negative which is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>Na</mi></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></msubsup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>71</mn></math></p><p>So, the correct option is C.</p>",
